faq:
  - q: What brand of industrial DTG printers does Silverscreen Decoration & Fulfillment use?
    lead: We use Brother GTX industrial printers for all our Direct-to-Garment (DTG) printing services.
    a: These state-of-the-art machines allow us to produce high-clarity, photorealistic images with fine detail and vibrant color palettes. Combined with our 20+ years of printing experience, Brother GTX technology ensures your custom merchandise meets the highest standards of quality.
  - q: How does Silverscreen handle garment pretreatment, and will it leave a stain?
    lead: We apply garment pretreatment using dedicated, separate equipment and guarantee that our process will not leave any stains on your apparel.
    a: Pretreatment is essential for the water-based inks to bond correctly with the fabric. Our meticulous quality control ensures a flawless, soft-feel finish every time, protecting your brand's integrity.
  - q: What fabric compositions are best for DTG printing vibrancy?
    lead: For optimal vibrancy and print quality, we exclusively support 100% cotton garments for our DTG printing services.
    a: Water-based DTG inks bond directly with natural cotton fibers. This ensures superior color reproduction and results in a soft, breathable finish that feels like an integral part of the fabric itself, rather than a heavy layer on top.
  - q: How many washes will a DTG printed garment last?
    lead: Our DTG prints offer exceptional wash-fastness and are tested to last for over 100 washes without significant fading.
    a: By utilizing premium water-based inks on 100% cotton apparel, the design embeds deeply into the fabric fibers. This guarantees maximum longevity and durability for your custom apparel.
  - q: How closely can DTG digital inks match my brand’s Pantone colors?
    lead: >-
      While DTG does not match Pantone colors quite as closely as <a href="/dtf">Direct-to-Film (DTF)</a> printing, our advanced RIP software allows us to match your brand colors exceptionally well.
    a: Our specialized software optimizes complex color palettes and subtle gradients, enabling us to reproduce your most intricate designs with high accuracy and visual impact.
  - q: Can DTG printing go over seams, zippers, or pockets?
    lead: No, DTG printing cannot be applied seamlessly over seams, zippers, or pockets.
    a: To achieve the highest clarity and sharpest detail, our Brother GTX printers require a completely flat printing surface. Printing over uneven elements compromises the ink application and final print quality.
  - q: Does Silverscreen integrate with e-commerce platforms for print-on-demand?
    lead: Yes, we integrate directly with major e-commerce platforms to provide seamless print-on-demand (POD) fulfillment services.
    a: This integration streamlines your entire decoration process, allowing you to scale your business and automate order processing efficiently while relying on a trusted fulfillment partner.
  - q: What are your DTG pricing brackets, and when is screen printing cheaper?
    lead: >-
      Our DTG pricing becomes more cost-effective at every dozen (12) quantity bracket, while <a href="/screen-print">screen printing</a> generally becomes the cheaper option for high-volume runs.
    a: >-
      Because each brand's needs vary, we recommend <a href="/contact-us">reaching out directly</a> for our detailed price lists. We will gladly help you determine the most economical printing method for your specific order volume.
  - q: Are the inks used in your DTG printing eco-friendly?
    lead: Yes, the water-based digital inks we use for DTG printing are fully eco-friendly and carry organic certifications.
    a: This ensures that your custom merchandise is not only vibrant and durable but also produced using environmentally responsible and safe manufacturing practices.
  - q: What is the standard turnaround time for a DTG apparel order?
    lead: Our standard turnaround time for single DTG orders is 5 to 7 days from the time the order is placed.
    a: If you need your garments sooner, expedited print-on-demand options are available in as little as 2 days at a higher price point. We consistently scale our production to meet your deadlines and keep your business moving forward.
---
